{#- The front door's hours sign (client 2026-10-31): replaces "Now Open", a
    month after opening, and is meant to be read from the parking lot.

    THE DAYS AND HOURS ARE THE SIGN. Landscape, because the door's glass is
    about 22in wide: 17in across takes the type about 1.6 times bigger than
    the old 11in-wide sign could. Lato Black, not Playfair: Playfair's thin
    strokes and old-style numerals are what go first at a distance.

    The logo is small because the window beside the door already carries the
    name. The QR and website are for whoever has walked up to the door. No
    street address: whoever reads the door is standing at it. -#}
{%- set o = site.opening %}
<div class="canvas sign door{% if bw %} sign--bw{% endif %}">
    <header class="door-mast">
        <div class="wordmark {{ 'wordmark--ink' if bw else 'wordmark--light' }}">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-display-italic door-kicker">Breakfast &amp; Lunch</p>
    </header>

    <div class="door-hours">
        <p class="door-days">{{ o.hoursDays }}</p>
        <p class="door-time">{{ o.opens.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.opens.meridiem }} &ndash; {{ o.closes.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.closes.meridiem }}</p>
        <p class="door-closed">Closed Saturday and Sunday</p>
    </div>

    {#- The QR encodes lvcafetogo.com/order (src/order.njk), so a change of
        ordering page never strands a printed code. -#}
    <footer class="door-foot">
        <div class="qr door-qr">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/qr-order.svg" %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-body door-order">Scan to <strong>order online</strong></p>
        <p class="p-body door-note">Lunch specials and soup from 11am</p>
        <p class="door-web">{{ site.social.website }}</p>
    </footer>
</div>
